{"metrics":{"latencyMs":3096},"output":{"message":{"content":[{"reasoningContent":{"reasoningText":{"text":"We need to answer with step-by-step reasoning for multiplication 17 * 23. Provide process: break down, use distributive property, maybe show long multiplication. Provide final answer."}}},{"text":"**Step‑by‑step multiplication of 17 × 23**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Write the numbers in a convenient order\nIt’s usually easier to multiply the larger number by the smaller one, but either way works.  \nWe’ll multiply **23** by **17**.\n\n```\n   23\n × 17\n ----\n```\n\n### 2. Multiply by the units digit (7)\n\n- 7 × 3 = 21 → write 1, carry 2.  \n- 7 × 2 = 14; add the carry 2 → 14 + 2 = 16.  \n\nSo the first partial product (for the 7) is **161**.\n\n```\n   23\n × 17\n ----\n  161   ← 7 × 23\n```\n\n### 3. Multiply by the tens digit (1), remembering its place value\n\nThe tens digit of 17 is **1**, but because it’s in the tens place we actually multiply by **10**.\n\n- 1 × 3 = 3 → write 3.  \n- 1 × 2 = 2 → write 2.\n\nNow shift this result one place to the left (add a zero) to reflect the factor of 10:\n\n```\n   23\n × 17\n ----\n  161   ← 7 × 23\n+ 230   ← 1 (i.e., 10) × 23\n```\n\n### 4. Add the two partial products\n\n```\n   161\n+  230\n-------\n   391\n```\n\n### 5. Result\n\n\\[\n17 \\times 23 = 391.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n#### Quick check with another method (distributive property)\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n17 \\times 23 &= (10+7) \\times (20+3) \\\\\n&= 10\\!\\times\\!20 \\;+\\; 10\\!\\times\\!3 \\;+\\; 7\\!\\times\\!20 \\;+\\; 7\\!\\times\\!3 \\\\\n&= 200 \\;+\\; 30 \\;+\\; 140 \\;+\\; 21 \\\\\n&= 391.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nBoth approaches give the same answer, confirming that **17 × 23 = 391**."}],"role":"assistant"}},"stopReason":"end_turn","usage":{"inputTokens":85,"outputTokens":551,"serverToolUsage":{},"totalTokens":636}}438 2300
